* Single-Transistor Boost — exported from Lutherie
* One silicon transistor in common emitter with a small emitter resistor: about 25 dB of gain, enough to push the next pedal or the amp into overdrive. The simplest pedal there is.

Vsig SIGSRC 0 SIN(0 0.3 220.0) AC 1
Rsig SIGSRC IN 1k
CC1 IN N2 100n
RR1 VCC_9V N2 430k
RR2 N2 0 43k
QQ1 N4 N2 N5 Q_2N5088
RR3 VCC_9V N4 10k
RR4 N5 0 390
CC2 N4 N6 100n
* Boost pot 100k A taper at 60%
RVR1a 0 OUT 16.2k
RVR1b OUT N6 83.8k
Rload OUT 0 1Meg
VVS1 VCC_9V 0 DC 9.0

.model Q_2N5088 NPN(Is=5.911e-15 Bf=1122.0 Br=1.271 Vaf=62.4 Nf=1.0 Cje=4.5e-12 Cjc=3e-12 Mje=0 Mjc=0)

.options reltol=1e-5 abstol=1e-13 vntol=1e-8 method=trap
.tran 1.3020833333333333e-06 0.3 0 1.3020833333333333e-06
.control
set wr_singlescale
set numdgt=12
run
wrdata single_transistor_boost.ngspice.txt v(OUT)
.endc
.end